{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507613-hunter-the-reckoning-5e-sub-forum","id":1507613,"title":"Hunter the Reckoning 5e sub-forum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-06T15:22:54-07:00","id":1507613,"title":"Hunter the Reckoning 5e sub-forum?","content":"Will there be a sub-forum of Hunter the Reckoning 5th Edition here? I see that it gets crapped on in reddit, but someone mentioned that elsewhere the game is loved by other people and I have no idea where other forums discuss about it with love and passion. I actually really like it myself and would like to see more people talk about it here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T16:31:38-07:00","id":1507624,"title":"","content":"No, sorry. Hunter 5 isn't one of our books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T09:40:30-07:00","id":1507695,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5\" data-vbnamecard=\"5\">RichT</a> Is it ok to discuss it in the general WoD forum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T10:55:23-07:00","id":1507699,"title":"","content":"Hunter: the Reckoning 5e also doesn't get much love here, and actually tends to get a lot of bashing for basically being a more restrictive version of Hunter: the Vigil 2e and having nonfunctional or vague rules (expect somebody to bring up Asset Edges). Which honestly makes a lot of sense, Hunter: the Vigil is <i>adored</i> and the second edition was basically one of OPP's most anticipated books (although generally considered slightly worse than 1e).<br /> <br /> Hunter: the Reckoning 1e is actually preferred here, due to having a more unique concept that fit with the satirical nature of WoD and, tbh, is more relevant (man I wish I'd kept my book). Imbued essentially ended up being one part fundamentalist army of god to three parts 4chan, which is at least more unique than yet another Modern Monster Hunting game. Imagine a continuation or reboot where hunter.net began drawing from modern internet trends, it would certainly be interesting.<br /> <br /> (Not that H5 can't bring in such elements, but they were part and parcel of HtR's assumptions about Western Imbued).<br /> <br /> <br /> It also doesn't help that Imbued can be added to HtV really easily (they're a Conspiracy connected by the internet and shared 'religious' experience) but not to H5. My draft has them calling themselves the Heirs of Gaia, and exist as a kind of internet subculture infesting various forums and social media platforms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T22:15:04-07:00","id":1507923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507613-hunter-the-reckoning-5e-sub-forum?p=1507699#post1507699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunter: the Reckoning 1e is actually preferred here, due to having a more unique concept that fit with the satirical nature of WoD and, tbh, is more relevant (man I wish I'd kept my book). Imbued essentially ended up being one part fundamentalist army of god to three parts 4chan, which is at least more unique than yet another Modern Monster Hunting game. Imagine a continuation or reboot where hunter.net began drawing from modern internet trends, it would certainly be interesting.<br /> <br /> (Not that H5 can't bring in such elements, but they were part and parcel of HtR's assumptions about Western Imbued).<br /> <br /> <br /> It also doesn't help that Imbued can be added to HtV really easily (they're a Conspiracy connected by the internet and shared 'religious' experience) but not to H5. My draft has them calling themselves the Heirs of Gaia, and exist as a kind of internet subculture infesting various forums and social media platforms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't the religious, occult, mystical, and supernatural experiences of the Messengers definitely more important and valueable to the Reckoning Hunters, compared to their digital communication logistics? From what I recall, the feelings and the visions received from their patrons could be said to be distinctly the main motif, topic, focus, and theme of these supplements and books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T02:55:57-07:00","id":1507926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507613-hunter-the-reckoning-5e-sub-forum?p=1507923#post1507923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't the religious, occult, mystical, and supernatural experiences of the Messengers definitely more important and valueable to the Reckoning Hunters, compared to their digital communication logistics? From what I recall, the feelings and the visions received from their patrons could be said to be distinctly the main motif, topic, focus, and theme of these supplements and books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a while since I've read the book, but the monster hunting 4chan stuff is what stuck in my head. Probably because religious hunters are pretty common, but a dedicated monster hunting forum is still a pretty unique element (I mean, Vigil touches on it with groups like Network Zero, but it's not a big thing the game puts focus on). Plus the Messenger stuff mostly happens to a <s>Solar</s> Imbued once or twice, whereas hunter.net should be a relatively everyday thing.<br /> <br /> Of course what they talk about online is being a fundementalist army of god, then the flame wars start. When it comes to Hunter you kind of can't separate the two.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing that struck me about H5, especially after completing Our For Blood and getting the Arcanum recruitment scene, is the switch in how hunters are presented compared to before it came out. Out For Blood is basically Hunter's Hunted the text adventure, including Numina (I've just started a run with five Faith) and presenting the Orgs more neutrally. Arcanum will make you a better hunter/paranormal researcher but will take you away from your life, with nothing in the game suggesting an ulterior motive (and I suspect the SI scene is the same, I've just not got it). Which honestly is a much better argument for disliking them than the one H5 actually gives, the fact that membership requires giving up the life you're trying to protect, but JA couldn't go with that because it's an offer some people will legitimately take.<br /> <br /> You know, at some point I'm going to get that CofD 1e Second Sight book, so I can run a game where hunters have hedge magic and faith in a system that isn't cWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T09:07:22-07:00","id":1519962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507613-hunter-the-reckoning-5e-sub-forum?p=1507926#post1507926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been a while since I've read the book, but the monster hunting 4chan stuff is what stuck in my head. Probably because religious hunters are pretty common, but a dedicated monster hunting forum is still a pretty unique element (I mean, Vigil touches on it with groups like Network Zero, but it's not a big thing the game puts focus on). Plus the Messenger stuff mostly happens to a <s>Solar</s> Imbued once or twice, whereas hunter.net should be a relatively everyday thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think our assumption, while writing the books back in the day, was that the majority of the Imbued weren\u2019t on hunter.net. This was an era when most people weren\u2019t online, yet. But, equally, most hunters weren\u2019t religious. They were small, isolated groups of people, with no help, minimal guidance from the Messengers, fighting a war they barely understood, and which was probably going to kill them. But they did it anyway. Because it was important. And there was nobody else. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27267-adders","name":"adders","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27267_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}